WEBVTT

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.390
Wait! Stella!

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.690
You know my feelings!

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:45.520
Let go of me!

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.520
S- Somebody!

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:48.860
Nobody can hear you.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.650
The beach is as lonely as you are!

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.260
Shit... That girl...

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.010
W- Who are you?

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.420
Mr. Sailor? Package for you.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:55.270
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:06.620
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:18.380
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:24.680
The weak person I was is no more

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.270
I decided to just believe

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:37.400
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.240
I go towards you

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:48.950
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:53.080
I go towards you

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:57.130
Blown by the wind

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:02.590
Oh blown

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:10.930
Melancholy Summer

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.250
Look at my head! You're so mean, Stella.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:33.410
It's because of you!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.920
It's because I love you! I want you!

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:38.750
Please go home.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:44.760
If I were to stop giving you side jobs, how would you survive?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:51.180
Nobody else on this island will give you work!

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:56.400
If you listen to me, I can buy you dresses, jewels, anything!

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.770
I don't belong to anyone...

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.530
I have a husband!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.860
And he abandoned you, didn't he?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.280
That's...

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.530
No matter how long you wait, he won't come back!

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.540
Stay away from me!

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.080
Stop!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.920
Ow! What the-

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:19.960
D...dear!

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:21.550
N... Nothing happened!

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.300
She's the one that seduced me!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.170
It's true!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:27.590
I can believe that.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:29.760
She is that type of woman after all.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.180
You know who her husband is.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:36.190
I offered her the job out of sympathy!

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.440
You little thief!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.990
Th... That's enough...

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:52.490
I'll never offer the likes of you a job again!

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:54.200
I hope you starve to death!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.830
Yeah yeah, starve to death, right?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.960
Now let's go home... You're heavy...

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.800
I heard that she seduced someone's husband.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:51.180
She doesn't look the type, but she's quite the harlot.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.510
She takes after her husband...

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:58.020
After all, it was her husband who ran away after killing two people!

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:13.910
This is a rather moody atmosphere for a tête-à-tête, don't you think...

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:16.540
Mr. Golgo 13.

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.920
Who is this man?

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.840
Arnold Glaston.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:30.420
He used to be an officer in our English Foreign Office,

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:36.010
and was secretly selling national secrets to some unscrupulous Russian companies.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:36.970
He's a traitor.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:40.270
The man who sold his country for money.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:47.070
We were beginning to catch onto him six years ago during the summer...

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:48.940
But he weaseled away.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:59.160
Whenever our agents travel abroad, they are under surveillance by SIS.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.460
With one exception:

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.290
The Honeymoon.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:09.460
Glaston pretended to fall in love with a girl and got married.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:14.470
After the wedding, he was given a clean escape to Malta.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.810
A few days later, the girl had served her purpose, and was abandoned in Malta.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.140
He escaped to his final destination: Russia.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:31.400
Two of our Malta branch officers caught scent of his plot, and tried to intercept him.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.200
They were killed.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:43.660
We managed to cover up the incident as a simple murder case, but only barely.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:50.760
The abandoned wife of a murderer now lives alone.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:54.930
A life of prejudiced stares from everyone on the island.

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:56.590
That girl...

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.430
She still lives on Malta?

00:08:58.430 --> 00:08:58.930
Correct.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:03.100
Six years ago, after Glaston's disappearance...

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.940
Why didn't she return to England?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.940
The fact remains she helped a traitor escape.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:14.950
And so you all prevented her return to England.

00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.860
Enough about the girl.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:21.450
Last month, Glaston was deported from Russia.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:28.330
No matter how many years pass, traitors must be taken care of.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.340
However...

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:31.460
His whereabouts are currently unknown.

00:09:32.300 --> 00:09:36.760
That's why, Mr. Golgo13, we offer you three million dollars,

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:38.840
to kill Glaston.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:43.020
You want me to aim at the target, but you don't know the location.

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:48.480
Of course we are using all our assets to look for him...

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:52.530
How many days did Glaston stay in Malta?

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:57.490
Malta? There is no possibility that Glaston would return to Malta.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:02.490
Not even for the girl. He used her as a tool for his escape.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.210
Glaston had no love in him to give.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.500
The number of days of their honeymoon?

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:16.550
Ten days.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.300
Ten days.

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:23.560
Ah...

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:25.140
This cabbage...

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.940
I'd like this cabbage please!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.020
We're sold out!

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.440
But you have so many!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:37.240
These are all reserved for respectable wives!

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:46.040
You lost your part-time job didn't you?

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.580
I'll find a new job!

00:10:48.910 --> 00:10:52.040
I'll pay the rent on time like always!

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.960
All right, I believe you.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:56.760
Just...

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:58.170
Thank heavens!

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:02.550
If you kicked me out, no one else would be willing to rent me a room.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.560
But you know...

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.060
Ahh, how do I say this...

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:28.410
Yo!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:38.170
Headquarters is worrying about you.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.680
They wonder how long you will stay in Malta.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:47.310
Glaston's hideout seems to be on the American West Coast.

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.890
So, you're being told to hurry up and fly over there.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.690
The West Coast... Seems to be?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.360
There are many conflicting reports.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:02.570
That is to say, the data on the United States is unreliable.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.410
Why do you keep observing the girl?

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:10.410
She was disposable.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.080
That woman is just like that..

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.630
Why does she stay in Malta?

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:27.850
It would be better if she tried returning to her home country, instead of waiting for a man who won't come back.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:33.690
Business is over. Please leave.

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.360
Well, I'll catch you later, buddy.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.700
Thank you very much.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:34.770
You're a hard man to find.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:40.020
As we thought, it's the West Coast after all.

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:42.820
He seems to be hiding out in Seattle.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.320
Is this definite?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:48.320
The branch is trying to confirm right now.

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:53.700
This means that the six years were futile..

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.080
You also struck out.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:04.170
Why you thought Glaston would return to her, I have no idea.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:11.430
I will inform you upon confirmation. Be ready to depart as soon as possible.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:27.730
<i>I'm old enough. I'm thinking about selling the land and settling down in Geneva where my son lives.</i>

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:32.200
The apartment... You'll sell it?

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.580
I am so very sorry...

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:38.410
But I have already decided to have the place demolished.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.490
If you don't catch me, I'll run far away!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.160
I...

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.290
I've had such a sad life, up till now.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.590
I can make you just as happy as you were sad.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.090
Oh Arnold...

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:36.320
Yes?

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.160
Are you Mrs. Glaston?

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:40.700
I am.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.120
You have a package.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:43.700
For me?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:46.290
Bye.

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:12.820
You're leaving right now?

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:17.740
I know this is sudden, but please clean my stuff from my room.

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:21.120
Thank you for the six years.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:24.580
Take care.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.060
S-

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:16.690
te-

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:18.190
lla.

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:46.220
The Job. It's finished.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.720
What was that?

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:53.060
I did my job. I promised I would tell you the results.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:56.020
Eh? So Glaston was in Malta?

00:20:56.690 --> 00:21:00.820
Call your Malta branch right away.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:04.200
Have them clear the body before someone sees it.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.110
Alright.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:08.620
But why did he go to Malta?

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:10.660
Ten days.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:13.830
Six years ago he stayed for ten days.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:19.840
He could have escaped to Russia right away, but he stayed.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.340
No way.

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:24.840
Glaston was serious about her? The tool of his escape?

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:39.120
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:44.670
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:53.560
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:55.890
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.890 --> 00:23:03.980
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:07.900
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:13.160
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:21.370
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.960
It was just a dream

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.380
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:34.390
In this calm night

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.640
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:41.770
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:47.730
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:54.200
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:02.210 --> 00:24:06.840
Mario hires Golgo to avenge his family's death.

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:13.430
To distract his enemies, Golgo goes by himself to the upper reaches of the Amazon.

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:18.680
On the jungle stage, an all out battle starts.

00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:21.640
Next time, on Golgo13:

00:24:20.350 --> 00:24:26.150
Garimpeiro

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:23.520
Garimpeiro

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:28.270
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
